cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Nosir
    given-names: Mohamed
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # replace with your ORCID
title: "Ammonia-AI: Physics-Informed Machine Learning for Nitrogen Adsorption Energy Prediction"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-07-01
url: "https://github.com/mohamednosir/ammonia-ai"  # replace with your GitHub URL
license: MIT
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - heterogeneous catalysis
  - nitrogen adsorption
  - ammonia synthesis
  - OC20
  - Sabatier volcano
  - generalized coordination number
  - d-band theory
abstract: >
  A physics-informed ML pipeline for predicting N* adsorption energies on
  transition metal surfaces using the OC20 IS2RE dataset. Combines
  d-band electronic descriptors with generalised coordination number (GCN)
  geometry features. Achieves MAE = 0.778 eV and CV R² = 0.557 on 5,047
  metallic *N systems, reproducing the Hammer-Nørskov Sabatier volcano ordering.
  Includes a rigorous GCN leakage analysis showing that initial-frame GCN
  outperforms final-frame GCN in alloy systems.

